  "project_description": "Back to top \n\n Overview \n Provides a media-type for webforms, allowing site-builders to configure the media-embed input filter so that content-editors can embed webforms in CKEditor.\n\n The project implements a new media type source, so a new media type bundle is set up with the source.\n\n Users then create new media, where each media has a reference field pointing to a Webform.\n\n The webform media can then be embedded as you would with any other media, via CKE's Media Library button.\n\n For more guidance, including configuration and installation, see the README.\n\n Back to top \n\n Features \n Provides a webform media type\n\n Back to top \n\n Requirements \n \n Webform module \n Media and Media Library modules in core \n \n Back to top \n\n Known problems \n None, please use the issue queue to report issues.\n\n Back to top \n\n Credits \n Written by Lee Rowlands of PreviousNext \n\n Back to top",
